00:26:21.510 --> 00:26:28.170
and he got a broadcast acceptable, I guess, format for this camera.

626
00:26:28.410 --> 00:26:33.690
It was 1080 progressive at 24 frames per second.

627
00:26:33.690 --> 00:26:38.490
So, anything they recorded on that camera was suitable for broadcaSt.

628
00:26:39.030 --> 00:26:39.550
1080p.

629
00:26:40.630 --> 00:26:41.150
1080p.

630
00:26:41.810 --> 00:26:43.890
Yeah, I see that on my TV sometimes.

631
00:26:44.130 --> 00:26:44.250
Yeah.

632
00:26:44.550 --> 00:26:45.610
Right, right.

633
00:26:45.930 --> 00:26:46.990
That's what that is.

634
00:26:47.810 --> 00:26:48.330
Okay.

635
00:26:50.010 --> 00:26:53.270
Ultimately, we only used two images from that camera.

